  data: {
    LLM: "If your starting rank is high (Aces or Kings), you can be more aggressive in early betting. If your rank is low, you should 'check' and 'call' to stay in the game for the Lowndpot half.\n\nThe Fold Decision: If two cards of your rank are discarded early (because they were dealt as initial cards to others or flipped before you), you cannot win the Highndpot. You must then pivot to having the lowest total hand or fold to minimize losses.\n\nPot Odds: Calculate how many 'live' cards are left for your rank versus your opponents. If you have 3 cards and there is only 1 left in the deck, but your opponent has 1 and 3 left, your odds of hitting Four-of-a-Kind are significantly higher.",
    Player: "If your starting rank is high (Aces or Kings), you can be more aggressive in early betting. If your rank is low, you should 'check' and 'call' to stay in the game for the Lowndpot half.\n\nThe Fold Decision: If two cards of your rank are discarded early (because they were dealt as initial cards to others or flipped before you), you cannot win the Highndpot. You must then pivot to having the lowest total hand or fold to minimize losses.\n\nPot Odds: Calculate how many 'live' cards are left for your rank versus your opponents. If you have 3 cards and there is only 1 left in the deck, but your opponent has 1 and 3 left, your odds of hitting Four-of-a-Kind are significantly higher.",
